### To-Do API — testes rápidos (extensão REST Client do VS Code)
### Rode a API antes: F5 no VS Code, ou `python app.py`

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:5000
@username = itamar
@password = senha-forte-123

### Saúde da API
GET {{baseUrl}}/ping

### Criar usuário
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{username}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Login (guarda o token na variável abaixo)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{username}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### Listar tarefas
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Listar só as concluídas
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks?done=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Criar tarefa
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Estudar Flask",
  "description": "Fechar o passo 5 do roteiro"
}

### Buscar tarefa por id
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Substituir a tarefa inteira (PUT)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tasks/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Estudar Flask com calma",
  "description": "Revisar JWT",
  "done": false
}

### Atualizar só um campo (PATCH)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tasks/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "done": true
}

### Apagar tarefa
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tasks/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Sem token — deve responder 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
